The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
rga->cmdbuf_virt = dma_alloc_attrs(rga->dev, RGA_CMDBUF_SIZE, &rga->cmdbuf_phy, GFP_KERNEL, DMA_ATTR_WRITE_COMBINE);
rga->src_mmu_pages = (unsigned int *)__get_free_pages(GFP_KERNEL | __GFP_ZERO, 3);
rga->dst_mmu_pages = (unsigned int *)__get_free_pages(GFP_KERNEL | __GFP_ZERO, 3);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the code does not check if the memory allocation functions `dma_alloc_attrs()` and `__get_free_pages()` fail, which can lead to dereferencing null pointers later in the code. Additionally, if `video_register_device()` fails, the code does not clean up previously allocated resources, leading to memory leaks and potential use-after-free errors.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!rga->cmdbuf_virt) {
    ret = -ENOMEM;
    goto rel_vdev;
}
if (!rga->src_mmu_pages) {
    ret = -ENOMEM;
    goto free_dma;
}
if (!rga->dst_mmu_pages) {
    ret = -ENOMEM;
    goto free_src_pages;
}
```
Reason:
The fix introduces checks for the return values of the memory allocation functions. If any of these allocations fail, the code sets an error code and jumps to the appropriate cleanup labels to free previously allocated resources, thus preventing memory leaks and use-after-free errors.

